    description: "The 8 dampening passes in ranking.py (apply_tier_weights, apply_noise_weights, apply_utility_symbol_weights, apply_common_method_name_weights, apply_sibling_impl_weights, apply_trivial_sink_weights, apply_generated_code_weights, apply_file_kind_weights) are all applied by rank_symbols. Three other symbol-selection surfaces compose their own subsets:\n\n- sketch._format_symbols (Key Symbols) applies 3 of 8 pre-centrality (tier, utility, trivial-sink); missing noise, common-method, sibling-impl, generated-code, file-kind.\n\n- compact.select_by_coverage applies 1 of 8 pre-centrality (tier, conditional on first_party_priority); missing 7.\n\n- compact.select_by_connectivity (used by format_tiered_behavior_map and the connectivity branch of format_compact_behavior_map) applies 0 pre-centrality. format_tiered_behavior_map then uses tier-weights *post-selection* for removal-ordering tiebreaking, which does not influence which symbols are selected.\n\nThe asymmetry is not architecturally justified - it is the residue of organic growth: each dampener was added to rank_symbols when its motivating bakeoff signal was filed, and the surface-level selectors were never backfilled. The sibling commit 7923615524 (\"unify symbol scoring across rank_files, cmd_symbols, and sketch\") was a partial fix at the file-scoring layer plus the extraction of filter_edges_for_ranking; the symbol-selection layer was not addressed. Note: edge-type weighting is a parameter of compute_centrality, not a behaviour of filter_edges_for_ranking - the filter only excludes test edges. Surfaces that want rank_symbols-equivalent edge weighting must wire edge_type_weights into their own compute_centrality calls.\n\nThis item splits into two phases.\n\nPhase A (audit). Deliverable: a structured 8x4 matrix (rows = the 8 dampeners; columns = sketch._format_symbols, compact.select_by_coverage, compact.select_by_connectivity, format_tiered_behavior_map). Each cell takes one of:\n  - apply        - dampener fixes a real FP class on this surface; backfill in Phase B.\n  - skip-noop    - dampener is a no-op given the surface's pre-filtering (e.g., file-kind dampener on a surface that already filters file-kind symbols). Document the skip in the surface's module docstring.\n  - skip-cost    - dampener is FP-positive but its wall-clock cost on this surface (which may run on every `hypergumbo .` invocation) does not justify the FP improvement. Document the skip with the measured cost.\n  - apply-post   - dampener applies post-selection only (the existing format_tiered_behavior_map tier-weights pattern; this is the baseline cell, included so any new post-selection uses are explicit).\n\nMethodology per cell:\n  1. FP-volume movement - run hypergumbo on a fixed corpus and compare top-N selected symbols with vs. without the missing dampener.\n  2. Wall-clock cost - measure per-dampener wall-clock on each surface, averaged over >=3 runs on the same corpus. apply_sibling_impl_weights and apply_noise_weights are graph-traversal-heavy; sketch Key Symbols runs on every `hypergumbo .` invocation, so cost matters here in a way it does not for `hypergumbo run`.\n\nPhase B (backfill). For each \"apply\" cell from Phase A, add the dampener call to the surface's selection pipeline. Re-run the bakeoff to confirm no regression. Per-cell PRs are acceptable; one consolidated PR is also fine.\n\nSurfaces involved (function names - line numbers omitted to survive refactor):\n  - sketch._format_symbols           (Key Symbols selector)\n  - compact.format_compact_behavior_map -> compact.select_by_coverage\n  - compact.format_compact_behavior_map -> compact.select_by_connectivity\n  - compact.format_tiered_behavior_map  -> compact.select_by_connectivity + post-selection apply_tier_weights\n\nOut of scope for this item:\n  - Refactoring rank_symbols' interface or extracting a compute_dampened_centrality helper (filed as the sibling stub WI-tahum-pipag-pavol-tarid-zofut-sahag-novob-rakip; this audit isbefore that one).\n  - Changes to selection logic on top of centrality (budgets, language proportionality, BFS-frontier connectivity) - those are surface-specific by design.\n  - Touching the file-level scoring path (rank_files / compute_file_scores / compute_symbol_importance_density) - already unified by 7923615524.\n  - Moving edge-type weighting out of compute_centrality.\n\nSide effects expected:\n  - Likely closes INV-mahap (entrypoint ranking utility bias) once apply_utility_symbol_weights is consistently applied across all entrypoint-touching surfaces. Confirm at PR time and add the resolution-rationale discussion entry per AGENTS.md.\n  - May reveal that some \"missing\" dampeners are actually intentional skips (skip-noop or skip-cost). Document those as the audit's findings and update the surface's module docstring.\n\nValidation:\n  - Bakeoff (BROAD or DEEP, whichever is most active) before/after on the same cohort. Tag awaits_bakeoff_validation at PR time per the bakeoff-validation discipline (not at filing time).\n  - Per-surface unit tests: each surface's selection function should produce the same output before/after for inputs where the missing dampener is a no-op (sanity), and different output when the dampener has bite.\n\nReferences:\n  - Original analysis: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04272026_1620.md\n  - Sibling spec-author question journal: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04272026_1545.md\n  - Half-finished prior unification: commit 7923615524\n  - ADR-0005 (sketch budget allocation) - describes Key Symbols selection intent without addressing dampener composition\n  - ADR-0012 (pass unification) - orthogonal to ranking, about analyzer/linker registration"  # 7976
